        "source_sentence": "To a 100-mL round-bottomed flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, a thermometer, nitrogen inlet and out tubes. 0.01 mol diamines, 15 mL of N,Ndimethylacetamide (DMAC), and 1 mL tertiary amide as the absorbent of HCl were added. Into the resulting suspension were added 5 mL DMAC and 0.01 mol 2,6- bis(4-chloroformylphenoxy)benzonitrile (ClPOBN). The reaction mixture was stirred at $0 ~ ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$for 1 h and warmed to room temperature for 2–3 h. Then the mixture of 0.74 g $\\mathrm { C a ( O H ) } _ { 2 }$and 5 mL DMAC were added to neutralize HCl."
